														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1786852">
									

<p>I think this is a good addition to the Circus, Berggren. You've got an upvote.</p>
<p>In related news, Cinicage was the first to rate and comment on this article, and he feels accomplished. Sources speculate that he will now get off of the SCP Foundation wiki for the night, and go to sleep because he is tired as fuck.</p>
<p>EDIT: Now that I'm awake and my posts can be a little more coherent, I'll tell you what I enjoy about this.</p>
<p>I like Uriel's character, I think of him as very lively and kind.</p>
<p>I really like the interview log. Like Roget said, it does say alot, I feel it adds a little more to how the Circus looked 'backstage', if you will.</p>
<p>One thing I found a tad unnerving in the interview was this line:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1834: (chuckling) I don't know what you could mean, sir. My sight is fine.</p>
<p>(Five seconds of silence, during which SCP-1834 retracts his right eyestalk slowly.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The way it's worded (&quot;SCP-1834 retracts his right eyestalk slowly.&quot;) makes me feel uncomfortable, in a good way.</p>

